.TH GENETREE 1 2000-1月 "steady_state" "steady_state"
.SH NAME
steady_state \- Solve the control steady state of the network, i.e. the "attractor" of the fitted
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIsteady_state(\fBtree\fR as <generic> XGBoostGRN, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Solve the control steady state of the network, i.e. the "attractor" of the fitted
 dynamical system when no intervention is applied.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBtree\fB \fR\- the trained [XGBoostGRN](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GeneTree.XGBoostGRN) model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a list with the slots \fBgene_names\fR and \fBmeans\fR: the difference between the
 mean and the wildtype baseline is the systematic drift of the tree model itself,
 which could be subtracted from the perturbation result.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the result is cached in the model object, the first call runs the fixed point
 iteration and the later calls are cheap. When an expression context is applied,
 the control steady state starts from the context state.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneTree
.SH FILES
.PP
